@* The dialog shown while the web interface's connection to the server is down, replacing the unstyled one
   Blazor injects by default (issue #39). Blazor finds it by its id, adds a class per state
   (components-reconnect-show, -retrying, -failed, -paused, -resume-failed, -rejected) and raises
   components-reconnect-state-changed on it; ReconnectModal.razor.js opens, closes and words it.

   Rendered statically from App, not interactively: it has to be in the page when the connection
   isn't there to render it. *@
<script type="module" src="@Assets["_content/Riftcaster.WebUI/Layout/ReconnectModal.razor.js"]"></script>

<dialog id="components-reconnect-modal" class="reconnect" aria-labelledby="reconnect-title" aria-describedby="reconnect-status">
    <div class="heading">
        <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2 id="reconnect-title" class="title">Connection to the server lost</h2>
    </div>

    @* Set by the script, once per state, so screen readers announce each state once. *@
    <p id="reconnect-status" class="status" role="alert">Reconnecting to the server…</p>
    @* Not part of the alert: it counts down every second. *@
    <p id="reconnect-countdown" class="countdown"></p>

    @* Only while Riftcaster is moving to another port (PortMoveNotice): the page can't reconnect to the old address,
       so it goes to the new one, and says how to if it can't. *@
    <p id="reconnect-move" class="move" hidden>If this page doesn't move by itself, <a id="reconnect-move-link" href="#">open the new address</a>.</p>

    <p class="note">Overlays will continue showing their most recent information and will automatically reconnect when possible.</p>

    <div class="actions">
        <button type="button" id="reconnect-retry" class="primary">Try again</button>
        <button type="button" id="reconnect-resume" class="primary">Resume</button>
        <button type="button" id="reconnect-reload" class="button-secondary">Reload page</button>
    </div>
</dialog>
